{
  "rationale": "Evidence from the last race (iteration 0, 60 trials) is consistent across all three development tracks. Every run ended off_track, with progress only 0.10 to 0.14, one line-loss event each, and max_error about 0.06 m, which is exactly the off-track limit. Steering oscillation was low (0.07 to 0.14), so the controller is not jittering. The robot is losing the line early and drifting away, not oscillating itself. Because completion is worth 500 points and progress alone is worth at most 250, survival comes before speed.\n\nDiagnosis: at base_speed 1.6 (PWM about 3276) the robot covers ground faster than the 0.04 m-half-width sensor bar can correct. The outer sensors sit 0.046 m from centre at most, so line loss starts before the controller has turned enough. The contract's speed target of about 1.5 m/s is therefore not safe with this sensing and gain set.\n\nChanges (one race, two controller fields):\n1. base_speed 1.6 to 1.3. This lowers the forward demand so the correction has more time to act on each bend. Per the Evaluator's guidance (leaves track, so lower base_speed), this is the primary fix.\n2. kd 0.15 to 0.3. Oscillation is low, so there is room for more damping. This follows the Evaluator's rule to raise kd when handling is the issue, and damps the response to changes in signal on the bends.\n\nKept fixed for attribution: kp 3.0, ki 0.05, sensor geometry, sensor_weights, line_loss 'last_direction'.\n\nExpected result: the robot should stay on the line longer, with progress well above 0.14 and fewer line-loss events. It may still not finish in 3 s at 1.3, which is acceptable if progress rises sharply. Completion time is the next target, and a later iteration can raise speed again once the run completes.\n\nHypotheses to test next: (H1) the off-track failure is speed-driven, so progress will rise substantially at 1.3. (H2) if progress still stalls near the first bend, the sensor span (+/-0.04 m) is too narrow and the next step is widening it to +/-0.06 m. (H3) kp 3.0 may be too weak to turn at the sharpest bend, which the next race would show via max_error at that bend.\n\nMeasurements wanted: completion, progress, completion_time, rms_error, max_error, line_loss_events, steering_oscillation. Per-track progress and the step at which the first line loss occurs would show whether it happens at start or on a specific bend.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.04}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.1,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.7
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.3,
    "kp": 3.0,
    "ki": 0.05,
    "kd": 0.3,
    "sensor_weights": [-2.0, -1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Slower, more damped run",
      "notes": "Cuts base_speed from 1.6 to 1.3 and doubles kd to 0.3, with geometry and kp fixed, because all 60 prior trials went off track at progress 0.10 to 0.14 with low oscillation. Speed is the main lever, so this tests whether the robot can stay on the line."
    }
  }
}
